---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Toc from '../components/Toc.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE, SITE_URL } from '../consts';

const updated = '4 September 2026';

/** Hand-written because the sections are hand-written; must match the <h2> ids below. */
const headings = [
	{ depth: 2, slug: 'overview', text: 'Overview' },
	{ depth: 2, slug: 'collect', text: 'What we collect' },
	{ depth: 2, slug: 'use', text: 'How we use it' },
	{ depth: 2, slug: 'analytics', text: 'Analytics and cookies' },
	{ depth: 2, slug: 'storage', text: 'What your browser stores' },
	{ depth: 2, slug: 'third-party', text: 'Third parties' },
	{ depth: 2, slug: 'security', text: 'Data security' },
	{ depth: 2, slug: 'choices', text: 'Your choices' },
	{ depth: 2, slug: 'changes', text: 'Changes to this policy' },
	{ depth: 2, slug: 'contact', text: 'Contact' },
];

const ld = {
	'@context': 'https://schema.org',
	'@type': 'WebPage',
	name: `Privacy Policy | ${SITE_TITLE}`,
	url: `${SITE_URL}/privacy/`,
	dateModified: '2026-09-04',
};
---

<Base
	title={`Privacy Policy | ${SITE_TITLE}`}
	description={`How ${SITE_TITLE} handles your data: what we collect, what we don't, the analytics we run, and what stays in your own browser.`}
	noNudge
>
	<script type="application/ld+json" slot="head" set:html={JSON.stringify(ld)} />

	<PageHero
		crumbs={[{ name: 'Privacy Policy' }]}
		eyebrow="Legal"
		title="Privacy *policy*"
		lead="The short version: you can read this whole site without an account, and we never sell anything about you. Here is the long version."
	>
		<p class="hero-meta meta"><Icon name="calendar" size={13} /> Last updated {updated}</p>
	</PageHero>

	<div class="container legal">
		<article class="prose legal__body">
			<div class="tldr">
				<p class="tldr__title"><Icon name="info" size={15} /> In one paragraph</p>
				<p>
					We ask for your email only if you subscribe to the brief. We run Google Analytics, which sets cookies
					and counts page views. Your saved tools, chosen angles and theme live in your own browser, not on our
					servers. We don't sell or rent personal information, and there is no advertising network on this site.
				</p>
			</div>

			<h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
			<p>
				This page explains what happens to information when you use <strong>{SITE_TITLE}</strong>
				(<a href={SITE_URL}>{SITE_URL}</a>) — what we collect, why, who else can see it, and how to get rid of it.
				It applies to the whole site, including the brief, the Toolbox, the newsletter and our forms.
			</p>
			<p>
				{SITE_TITLE} is a static website. There is no login, no user account and no profile attached to you.
			</p>

			<h2 id="collect">What we collect</h2>
			<p><strong>Email address.</strong> If you subscribe to the newsletter, we collect the email address you type in,
				solely to send you the brief and related updates. Subscription is handled by our email provider, and every
				email carries a one-click unsubscribe link.</p>
			<p><strong>What you send us in a form.</strong> If you contact us or submit a tool, we receive whatever you put in
				the form — typically your name, your email address and your message — so that we can reply and, in the case
				of a listing, review the tool.</p>
			<p><strong>Payment details for a listing.</strong> We never see or store card numbers. Listing payments are taken by
				Polar, our merchant of record; we receive a confirmation containing the checkout reference and the email you
				paid with.</p>
			<p><strong>Usage data.</strong> We collect aggregate analytics about pages visited, approximate location at country
				level, referring URLs and device type. This is used in aggregate to see which pages are worth keeping, and it
				is not used to build a profile of you.</p>
			<p>We do not ask for, and have no use for, your date of birth, your phone number or your address.</p>

			<h2 id="use">How we use it</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>To send the newsletter you asked for, and nothing else you didn't.</li>
				<li>To reply to messages and review tools submitted for listing.</li>
				<li>To understand which briefs, explainers and tool pages people actually read, so we can write more of what works.</li>
				<li>To keep the site up, fast and free of abuse.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				We do not sell, rent or trade personal information. We do not run an advertising network, and nothing on this
				site retargets you elsewhere.
			</p>

			<h2 id="analytics">Analytics and cookies</h2>
			<p>
				This site runs <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> (measurement ID <code>G-XP68CXTJCM</code>) on every page.
				Google Analytics sets its own cookies in your browser and records a page view, the referring page, your
				device type and an approximate location derived from your IP address. Earlier versions of this policy said
				the site used no cookies; that was inaccurate, and this section replaces it.
			</p>
			<p>
				We use the reports in aggregate only — we never attempt to identify an individual reader, and we do not
				upload email addresses or any other personal identifiers to Google Analytics.
			</p>
			<p>
				If you would rather not be counted, you can block analytics with a content blocker or your browser's tracking
				protection, use Google's <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">opt-out add-on</a>,
				or enable "Do Not Track". Blocking analytics does not break anything on this site.
			</p>

			<h2 id="storage">What your browser stores</h2>
			<p>
				A few small things are kept in your own browser's local storage so the site remembers your preferences between
				visits. They never leave your device, we cannot read them, and clearing your site data removes them:
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li>your light/dark theme choice;</li>
				<li>the tools you have saved, and any comparison you have started;</li>
				<li>the brief angles you picked, your reading streak and the date of your last visit;</li>
				<li>whether you have already subscribed, so we stop nudging you.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				A tool submission is also held briefly in your browser's session storage between the form and the payment step,
				so that the details survive the trip to the checkout page. It is discarded when you close the tab.
			</p>

			<h2 id="third-party">Third parties</h2>
			<p>Only these services receive data, and only for what they do:</p>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Beehiiv</strong> — delivers the newsletter, and stores your email address for that purpose.</li>
				<li><strong>Formspree</strong> — passes contact and submission forms to our inbox.</li>
				<li><strong>Polar</strong> — takes listing payments as merchant of record and handles cancellations.</li>
				<li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> — aggregate traffic measurement, as described above.</li>
				<li><strong>Vercel</strong> — hosts and serves the site, and keeps standard server logs.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				Each of these processes data under its own privacy policy. We link out to hundreds of AI tools; once you follow
				a link, that site's own policy applies and this one no longer does.
			</p>

			<h2 id="security">Data security</h2>
			<p>
				The site is served over HTTPS, and we take reasonable measures to protect the limited information we hold.
				No method of transmission or storage over the internet is completely secure, so we cannot promise absolute
				security — which is also why we deliberately collect as little as possible.
			</p>

			<h2 id="choices">Your choices</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Unsubscribe</strong> from any newsletter email, in one click.</li>
				<li><strong>Ask for a copy</strong> of what we hold about you, or ask us to delete it, by emailing us. We will action it within 30 days.</li>
				<li><strong>Opt out of analytics</strong> using the methods above.</li>
				<li><strong>Clear your site data</strong> in your browser to wipe everything stored locally.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				This site is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect information from them.
			</p>

			<h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
			<p>
				We may update this policy from time to time. When we do, we revise the "last updated" date at the top of this
				page. Material changes — like the analytics disclosure above — are described in the section they affect rather
				than quietly edited in.
			</p>

			<h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
			<p>
				Questions about any of this, or a request about your data: use the
				<a href="/contact/">contact form</a> or email <a href="mailto:hello@getaibriefs.com">hello@getaibriefs.com</a>.
				See also our <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a>.
			</p>
		</article>

		<aside class="legal__aside">
			<Toc headings={headings} title="On this page" />
		</aside>
	</div>
</Base>

<style>
	.hero-meta { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }

	.legal {
		display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 220px; gap: var(--s-16);
		align-items: start;
		padding-block: clamp(2rem, 1.6rem + 2.4vw, 3.5rem) var(--section);
	}
	.legal__body { max-width: 68ch; }
	.legal__aside { position: sticky; top: calc(var(--header-h, 64px) + 32px); }
	@media (max-width: 1040px) {
		.legal { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: var(--s-8); }
		.legal__aside { position: static; order: -1; padding-bottom: var(--s-4); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
	}

	.tldr {
		background: var(--surface-2); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--r-md);
		padding: var(--s-5); font-size: var(--text-base); line-height: 1.65;
	}
	.tldr__title {
		display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; margin-bottom: var(--s-2);
		font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.6875rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase;
		font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent-ink);
	}
	.tldr p:last-child { color: var(--ink-2); margin: 0; }

	.prose h2 { font-size: var(--text-xl); padding-top: var(--s-2); }
	.prose code { font-size: 0.85em; }
</style>
